** SCOPE CAVEAT, stated explicitly (not glossed over): every number in this
script is a Cramer-Rao bound under IDEALIZED, uncorrelated Gaussian measurement
noise at the project's ASSUMED (not independently validated, per Session 2/4's
own flags) SIGMA_NEFF/SIGMA_NG. It is a best-case, information-theoretic bound,
not a real nonlinear-fit result. The literature-cited compact-modeling paper
(project_brief.md) found a REAL extraction procedure's fit residual stayed flat
across 85-90deg sidewall angle -- that is a statement about a specific realistic
fitting procedure under real (correlated, non-Gaussian, model-uncertain) noise,
not a Fisher-information CRB. The absolute CRB numbers here (all sub-degree,
even for strip alone) should NOT be read as 'the angle problem is already solved
without rib' -- the RELATIVE comparison (rib gives the largest angle-specific
improvement of the structures tested, 11-51x depending on budget/assumption) is
the robust, actionable finding; the absolute sub-degree numbers reflect how
optimistic the assumed noise floor is, a pre-existing project assumption this
session did not re-derive.
